\p \v 1 \w Early in the morning|strong="H07925"\w* \w Jerubbaal|strong="H03378"\w*\f + \fr 7:1 \fqa Jerubbaal \ft is another name for \fqa Gideon \ft and probably means \fqa let Baal contend\ft ; see Judges 6:32.\f* \w (that is|strong="H01931"\w*, \w Gideon|strong="H01439"\w*) \w and all|strong="H03605"\w* \w the men|strong="H05971"\w* \w -|strong="H00834"\w* \w with him|strong="H00854"\w* \w camped|strong="H02583"\w* \w beside|strong="H05921"\w* \w vvv|strong="H05878"\w* \w the spring of Harod|strong="H05878"\w*. \w And the camp|strong="H04264"\w* \w of Midian|strong="H04080"\w* \w was|strong="H01961"\w* \w north|strong="H06828"\w* of them \w in the valley|strong="H06010"\w* \w near the hill|strong="H01389"\w* \w of Moreh|strong="H04176"\w*.
