\p \v 27 \w [From all this] Gideon|strong="H01439"\w* \w made|strong="H06213"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w an ephod|strong="H00646"\w*, \w which he placed|strong="H03322"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w in Ophrah|strong="H06084"\w*, \w his hometown|strong="H05892"\w*. \w But soon all|strong="H03605"\w* \w Israel|strong="H03478"\w* \w prostituted themselves|strong="H02181"\w* \w by worshiping it|strong="H00310"\w* \w there|strong="H08033"\w*, \w and it became|strong="H01961"\w* \w a snare|strong="H04170"\w* \w to Gideon|strong="H01439"\w* \w and his household|strong="H01004"\w*.
\s1 Forty Years of Peace
