\p \v 7 \w So the five|strong="H02568"\w* \w men|strong="H00582"\w* \w departed|strong="H01980"\w* \w and came|strong="H00935"\w* \w to Laish|strong="H03919"\w*, \w where they saw|strong="H07200"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w that the people|strong="H05971"\w* \w -|strong="H00834"\w* \w -|strong="H07130"\w* \w were living|strong="H03427"\w* \w securely|strong="H00983"\w*, \w like|strong="H04941"\w* \w the Sidonians|strong="H06722"\w*, \w quiet|strong="H08252"\w* \w and unsuspecting|strong="H00982"\w*. \w There was nothing|strong="H00369"\w* \w . . .|strong="H01697"\w* \w lacking|strong="H03637"\w* \w in the land|strong="H00776"\w* \w and no oppressive|strong="H03423"\w* \w ruler|strong="H06114"\w*. \w And they|strong="H01992"\w* \w were far away|strong="H07350"\w* \w from the Sidonians|strong="H06722"\w* \w and had no|strong="H00369"\w* . . . \w alliance|strong="H01697"\w* \w with|strong="H05973"\w* \w anyone|strong="H00120"\w*.
